brand: Burton
model name: Custom X
model year: 2027
SKU: 106891CE0BRG150
AUD price: $1,199.99
available lengths: 150cm, 154cm, 156cm, 158cm, 162cm, 158cm Wide, 162cm Wide, 166cm Wide
board type: All Mountain
park rating: 6/10
all mountain rating: 9/10
powder rating: 7/10
flex: 8/10 (1=soft, 10=stiff)
flex description: Stiff, precise, responsive, built for advanced riders tackling high speeds, steep terrain, or icy conditions
rider level: Advanced
shape: Directional/Twin
shape description: Directional shape with longer nose and shorter tail for control, stability, and float in powder; Twin Flex with symmetrical design for balance and versatility riding regular or switch
camber type: Camber (most aggressive board bend, unmatched power, response, edge control, powerful turns, poppy precision)
width: Standard, Wide
mounting system: The Channel (channel system for fine-tuned stance width and stance location, compatible with most major binding brands, works best with Burton EST bindings)
laminate: Triax with Carbon I-Beam
laminate detail - Triax: Fiberglass layered above and below the core for versatile flex and consistent response
laminate detail - Carbon I-Beam: Ultralight carbon backbone added to bottom layer of Triax fiberglass to increase pop
core: Dragonfly 600G Core with Multicore EGD and Squeezebox
core description - Dragonfly 600G: Stronger and lighter woods in specific areas for more pop and strength while reducing weight, end-grain woods in impact zones
core technology - Multizone EGD: Wood grain aligned along heel and toe edge in four separate zones adjacent to the channel, channeling power directly to edges for ultimate strength and edge control
core technology - Squeezebox: Thicker more powerful sections combined with thinner more flexible sections profiled throughout core for enhanced energy transfer, snappier and more stable board
edge technology: Frostbite Edges (edges extend out slightly underneath bindings for enhanced edge hold on hardpack and ice)
base: Sintered WFO (extra absorbent, high density sintered material infused with specially formulated wax, ultra durable)
durability technology: Infinite Ride (boards overbuilt in factory then broken down using machinery so board rides the same from day one to day 100, season after season)
tip/tail technology: Pro-Tip (tip and tail taper out at the points, reducing swing weight and promoting mobility)
resin: Super Sap Epoxy (bio-based resin that reduces carbon footprint by 50% over conventional petroleum-based epoxies)
shipping restriction: Only available for shipping within Australia
riding style: Aggressive all-mountain, steep backcountry lines, competition, high-speed carving
